    "notes": "From a Strat-O-Matic product photo in its WordPress media library (media item 7389, 'individual_team_card', 2592x1952; sourceUrl is the item's public REST record, sourceImage the file): four advanced cards fanned on a table. Conor Jackson's card lies on top, completely uncovered, about 1220 px wide, slightly rotated and in focus; every cell is sharp at native resolution. The other three cards (J.J. Hardy, C.J. Wilson, John Lackey) are partly covered and were not transcribed. Read twice: (1) from a native-resolution crop of the whole card, (2) from 1.8x crops of each platoon grid; no differences. Markers: diamond ◆, downTriangle ▼, upTriangle △ (LHP col2 roll3 and RHP col3 roll3, each printing 'SINGLE (..)' on the roll line and an italic 'SI* / lo (ss)' d20 split on the two lines directly beneath; binding unambiguous), omega Ω, '?' as questionMark, underlined class letters as 'underline:C'. Two splits print the class letter run into the range ('gb (3b) B9-20', 'gb (3b) B5-20'); raw inserts the space. 'plus injury' prints on its own line under HBP (LHP col1 roll2, RHP col3 roll12). YEAR IS INFERRED, not printed: the card fits Jackson's 2008 season (6 triples, 10 SB, 9 HBP: the card prints triples on both grids, a C steal rating and 3 HBP chances per grid, i.e. 2 x 9/612 PA x 108 = 3.2) and fits it closely (largest benchmark error .0075, triple rate exact), while 2007 (1B .029, BB .019, HR .011) and 2006 (SO .034) do not; the photo's other cards (C.J. Wilson as a reliever with a closer rating, Lackey a starter, Hardy at shortstop) fit the same season."
